I would have preferred not to wish for GDSM. I would have wished for
SDSM.
and got magic resistance through magic mirror of merlin. It is also not
a priority
till you reach DLvl7.

Yes blessed +3 Greyswandir is the best weapon for an Arch.

You may also want to wish for the magic mirror of merlin, since you
already
have magic resistence by the GDSM you can wish for it at only 20 hit
points.

Have you got poison resistance then wish for a blessed tin of green
dragon meat.
It is important to have this resistance. You don't want to die after
having such a
good luck.

Actually Speed boots are not that useful for Archealogists as they are
already fast.
They will come useful a little later, but by then you may get spell of
haste self.
So I would prefer a couple of magic markers, but I would wait till I
have seen scrolls
of enchant armour/enchant weapon. If I don't get them till I start to
see dangerous monsters
then wish for them along with one marker.
Any enchanted armour is good in the early game particularly elven.

